@*
    Blazor replacement for the WebForms server control
    "MixERP.Net.WebControls.ScrudFactory.ScrudForm" (formerly 17 partial files under ScrudForm/).

    THE RENDER TREE BELOW IS THE PORT OF, in this order:
      ScrudForm/Control.cs           CreateChildControls()   -> OnParametersSet + this markup
      ScrudForm/ScrudContainer.cs    LoadScrudContainer()    -> title, ruler, description,
                                                                command panels, grid panel,
                                                                form panel, update panel, script
      ScrudForm/Title.cs             AddTitle/AddRuler/AddDescription/LoadTitle/LoadDescription
      ScrudForm/ViewFactory/*        CreateGridPanel/AddGridView/AddLastValueHiddenField/
                                     BindGridView/LoadGrid
      ScrudForm/Pager.cs             CreatePager (both overloads)
      ScrudForm/FormFactory/*        CreateFormPanel/AddFormHeader/AddFormContainer/AddFormFooter,
                                     DisplayError/DisplaySuccess
      ScrudForm/UpdatePanel.cs       AddUpdatePanel/CreateCommandPanels/GetItemSelectorPath/
                                     GetResourceClassName
      ScrudForm/Styling.cs           the 27 css/style resolvers + GetPageSize/GetRowLimit
      ScrudForm/Validation.cs        Validate()  (renamed ValidateProperties() - see @code)

    THE DOM CONTRACT IS LOAD-BEARING. Scrud.js selects by LITERAL id: #GridPanel, #FormPanel,
    #FormGridView, #ScrudUpdatePanel, #ScrudError, #TitleLabel, #LastValueHidden, #UserIdHidden,
    #OfficeCodeHidden, #SaveButton, #CancelButton, #UseButton, #SelectRadio, and the suffixed
    #EditButtontop / #DeleteButtontop (hardcoded). #ScrudError must exist UNCONDITIONALLY because
    scrudOnServerError() writes into it, and #ScrudUpdatePanel must exist because scrudLayout()
    sizes it. Changing any of these compiles green and silently kills the feature.

    PUBLIC API IS FROZEN: MixERP.Net.FrontEnd declares "public sealed class Scrud : ScrudForm" and
    assigns UserId/UserName/OfficeCode/OfficeId/Catalog from its constructor, so this component
    must stay inheritable and those five members must stay plain settable [Parameter]s.
*@

@namespace MixERP.Net.WebControls.ScrudFactory
@inherits ComponentBase
@inject IJSRuntime JSRuntime
@inject NavigationManager Nav

@using System
@using System.Collections.Generic
@using System.ComponentModel
@using System.Data
@using System.Globalization
@using System.Reflection
@using System.Threading
@using System.Threading.Tasks
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.WebUtilities
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Primitives
@using Microsoft.JSInterop
@using MixERP.Net.Common
@using MixERP.Net.Common.Helpers
@using MixERP.Net.Framework
@using MixERP.Net.i18n.Resources
@using MixERP.Net.WebControls.Common
@using MixERP.Net.WebControls.ScrudFactory.Controls
@using MixERP.Net.WebControls.ScrudFactory.Data
@using MixERP.Net.WebControls.ScrudFactory.Helpers

@*
    Control.cs: PageUtility.AddMeta(this.Page, "generator", <assembly name>).
    The migrated overload is AddMeta(StringBuilder head, name, content) and returns the markup, so
    the tag is emitted through the host's head outlet instead of Page.Header. The meta tag is NOT
    dropped. See migration-summary note for task 82.
*@
<HeadContent>@((MarkupString)PageUtility.AddMeta(null, "generator", Assembly.GetAssembly(typeof(ScrudForm)).GetName().Name))</HeadContent>

@*
    Title.cs LoadTitle(): "this.Page.Title = this.Text". A library component cannot assign
    Page.Title, but <PageTitle> is the modern equivalent and keeps the behaviour rather than
    silently dropping it. A host that already renders its own <PageTitle> wins by order, exactly as
    a WebForms page that re-assigned Page.Title after the control ran did.
*@
@if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(this.Text))
{
    <PageTitle>@this.Text</PageTitle>
}

@* Control.cs: this.scrudContainer = new Panel() -> the outer div every piece is added to. *@
<div>
    @* Title.cs AddTitle(Panel): div(class = GetTitleLabelCssClass) > Label(ID = "TitleLabel"). *@
    <div class="@this.GetTitleLabelCssClass()">
        <span id="TitleLabel">@this.Text</span>
    </div>

    @* Title.cs AddRuler(Panel): HtmlGenericControl("div") with class "ui divider". *@
    <div class="ui divider"></div>

    @*
        Title.cs AddDescription + LoadDescription: the label got its css class and text ONLY when
        Description was non-empty, so an empty Description rendered an empty, class-less span.
        Emitting nothing in that case is the same visual result with less noise (task 21).
    *@
    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(this.Description))
    {
        <span class="@this.GetDescriptionCssClass()" style="display:block;">@this.Description</span>
    }

    @*
        UpdatePanel.cs AddUpdatePanel(Panel). The ASP.NET AJAX partial-postback machinery is gone
        (Blazor re-renders by itself), but the ELEMENT and its id stay: scrudLayout() in Scrud.js
        sizes #ScrudUpdatePanel.
    *@
    <div id="ScrudUpdatePanel">
        @* ContentTemplateContainer order: top command panel, message label, grid panel, form panel,
           bottom command panel, the two hidden fields. *@
        @this.topCommandPanel.GetCommandPanel("top")

        @*
            FormFactory/Alert.cs messageLabel. DisplayError() assigned ID = "ScrudError" at the
            moment it had something to say; the element is now rendered UNCONDITIONALLY because
            Scrud.js's scrudOnServerError() does $("#ScrudError").html(...) on an ajax failure and
            would otherwise write into nothing.
        *@
        <span id="ScrudError" class="@this.messageCssClass" style="@this.messageStyle">@this.messageText</span>

        @* ViewFactory/GridPanel.cs CreateGridPanel(). *@
        <div id="GridPanel" class="@this.GetGridPanelCssClass()" style="@this.GetGridPanelInlineStyle()">
            @*
                AddGridView(): the already-migrated MixERPGridView component (NOT a new GridView()).
                LoadGrid() additionally set the grid's Width and a white-space:nowrap inline style;
                MixERPGridView exposes neither, so both are carried on this wrapper div - recorded
                as a divergence (tasks 15/42).
            *@
            @*
                GridPanel.cs also set formGridView.RowStyle.CssClass = GetGridViewRowCssClass() and
                AlternatingRowStyle.CssClass = GetGridViewAlternateRowCssClass(). RowStyle and
                AlternatingRowStyle were inherited GridView members that MixERPGridView does not
                have (Common section 5.3), so - exactly as ScrudItemSelector already does - the two
                resolved values are surfaced as data-* hooks on this wrapper so host CSS can still
                stripe the rows. Dropping them would silently remove row striping for every
                consumer that configures these two scrud parameters.
            *@
            <div role="grid-wrapper" style="@this.GetGridViewInlineStyle()"
                 data-row-css-class="@this.GetGridViewRowCssClass()"
                 data-alternate-row-css-class="@this.GetGridViewAlternateRowCssClass()">
                <MixERPGridView ID="FormGridView"
                                CssClass="@this.GetGridViewCssClass()"
                                AutoGenerateColumns="false"
                                Columns="@this.gridColumns"
                                DataSource="@this.gridDataSource" />
            </div>

            @*
                AddLastValueHiddenField(): a TextBox with display:none and the literal id
                #LastValueHidden, which Scrud.js reads in scrudSaveAndClose().
            *@
            @*
                The value is rendered from component state because Save() writes the selected key
                (then the inserted key) into it - the port of
                "this.lastValueHiddenTextBox.Text = id".
            *@
            <input type="text" id="LastValueHidden" name="LastValueHidden" style="display:none;" value="@this.lastValue" />

            @* Control.cs: this.CreatePager(this.gridPanel) - the pager is the grid panel's last child. *@
            @this.pager
        </div>

        @* FormFactory/FormPanel.cs CreateFormPanel(). *@
        <div id="FormPanel" class="@this.GetFormPanelCssClass()" style="@(this.formVisible ? "display:block;" : "display:none;")">
            @*
                this.form = new Panel { CssClass = GetFormCssClass(), role = "form" }.
                The "loading" class is the port of the AjaxProgressTemplate spinner: Scrud.js's
                scrudDispalyLoading()/scrudRemoveLoading() add and remove exactly this class on
                #FormPanel div.segment, so driving it from component state uses the SAME affordance
                the client script uses and keeps both in step (task 33).
            *@
            <div class="@this.GetFormCssClass() @(this.busy ? "loading" : null)" role="form">
                @* AddFormHeader(): the required-field legend literal. *@
                <div class='form-description'>@Titles.RequiredFieldDetails</div>

                @*
                    AddFormContainer(): the panel LoadForm() filled with <table role="scrud">.
                    ScrudFactory.LoadForm (Specialist 4) populates this.fieldTable; the table itself
                    lives here, and every row is a ScrudFieldRow - the migrated per-column renderer.
                *@
                <div>
                    @if (this.fieldTable.Fields.Count > 0)
                    {
                        <table role="scrud">
                            <tbody>
                                @foreach (ScrudField f in this.fieldTable.Fields)
                                {
                                    <ScrudFieldRow Field="f" FieldChanged="this.OnFieldChanged" />
                                }
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    }
                </div>

                @* AddFormFooter(): a one-row table, label cell then control cell. *@
                <table>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="label-cell"></td>
                        <td class="control-cell">
                            @*
                                The Use button existed only in the modal branch, where the popup
                                hands the saved key back to its opener.
                            *@
                            @if (this.IsModal())
                            {
                                <button type="button" id="UseButton" class="@this.GetButtonCssClass()" @onclick="this.UseButton_Click">@Titles.Use</button>
                            }

                            @*
                                OnClientClick="return(scrudClientValidation());" was the client half
                                of the WebForms validation pipeline. The server-side gate
                                (ScrudFieldTable.Validate(), consumed by SaveButton_Click) is the
                                replacement and is authoritative; the handler still raises the
                                loading affordance the old OnClientClick raised.
                            *@
                            <button type="button" id="SaveButton" class="@this.GetSaveButtonCssClass()" @onclick="this.SaveButton_Click">@Titles.Save</button>

                            <button type="button" id="CancelButton" class="@this.GetButtonCssClass()" @onclick="this.CancelButton_Click">@Titles.Cancel</button>

                            @* HtmlInputReset: a native reset input, value = Titles.Reset. *@
                            <input type="reset" class="@this.GetButtonCssClass()" value="@Titles.Reset" />
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>

        @this.bottomCommandPanel.GetCommandPanel("bottom")

        @*
            UpdatePanel.cs: the two HiddenFields Scrud.js reads through the injected
            userIdHiddenId / officeCodeHiddenId globals.
        *@
        <input type="hidden" id="UserIdHidden" name="UserIdHidden" value="@this.UserId.ToString(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)" />
        <input type="hidden" id="OfficeCodeHidden" name="OfficeCodeHidden" value="@this.OfficeCode" />
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    //==================================================================================
    // SEAMS OWNED BY SPECIALIST 4 (checklist tasks 23, 25, 43, 44, 53-65, 80, 81).
    // This markup and the shell code below CALL the following members, which Specialist 4
    // adds to this same component. The exact signatures referenced are:
    //
    //   private Task SaveButton_Click()                     - task 54
    //   private Task UseButton_Click()                      - task 55
    //   private Task CancelButton_Click()                   - task 60
    //   private Task DeleteButton_Click()                   - task 58
    //   private Task EditButton_Click()                     - task 59
    //   private Task OnFieldChanged(ScrudField field)       - re-runs the task-65 gate
    //   private void LoadForm(DataTable values, bool editing)        - task 62
    //   private string GetLocalizedErrorMessage(MixERPException ex)  - task 23
    //   private void ResetForm()                            - task 25
    //   private RenderFragment<object> GetSelectColumnTemplate()     - task 43 (#SelectRadio)
    //   private string GetSelectedValue() / void ClearSelectedValue()- task 44
    //   [Parameter] public EventCallback SaveButtonClick / UseButtonClick - task 53
    //   AddScrudScript() from OnAfterRenderAsync(firstRender)        - tasks 80/81
    //
    // Shell state Specialist 4 consumes, declared below and ALREADY implemented here:
    //   this.fieldTable  (ScrudFieldTable - the FindControl replacement + validation gate source)
    //   this.imageColumn (the bytea column name, set while the form is generated)
    //   this.busy        (drives the #FormPanel div.segment "loading" class)
    //   this.formVisible / this.gridVisible, DisplayError/DisplaySuccess, GetResourceClassName,
    //   GetItemSelectorPath, GetRowLimit, GetPageSize and the 27 styling resolvers.
    //
    // NOTE on names: the legacy private Validate() (the PROPERTY guard, task 18) is renamed
    // ValidateProperties() here precisely so that the names Validate()/IsValid stay free for
    // Specialist 4's task-65 validation gate, which is what Page.Validate()/Page.IsValid become.
    //==================================================================================

    //==================================================================================
    // ScrudForm/Properties.cs - 52 [Parameter]s. EVERY NAME IS FROZEN: seven dependent
    // projects set them from markup, and FrontEnd/Controls/Scrud.cs sets five of them from a
    // subclass constructor, which is why they are plain settable properties as well.
    //==================================================================================

    [Parameter]
    public string AddButtonIconCssClass { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string AllButtonIconCssClass { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string ButtonCssClass { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string CommandPanelButtonCssClass { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string CommandPanelCssClass { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string CompactButtonIconCssClass { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    ///     Use this parameter to override the ScrudFactory's
    ///     default Add/Edit event implementation by redirecting to a custom url.
    ///     The edit event redirects to the custom url with the KeyColumn parameter
    ///     and the selected value appended as query string data.
